      <CodeBlock code={"2024-06-10T18:09:57.774Z|00016|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"BANP:default:Egress:0\", verdict=drop, severity=alert, direction=from-lport: tcp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:82:02:56,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:82:02:57,nw_src=10.130.2.86,nw_dst=10.130.2.87,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=64,nw_frag=no,tp_src=45614,tp_dst=8080,tcp_flags=syn\n2024-06-10T18:09:58.809Z|00017|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"BANP:default:Egress:0\", verdict=drop, severity=alert, direction=from-lport: tcp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:82:02:56,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:82:02:57,nw_src=10.130.2.86,nw_dst=10.130.2.87,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=64,nw_frag=no,tp_src=45614,tp_dst=8080,tcp_flags=syn\n2024-06-10T18:10:00.857Z|00018|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"BANP:default:Egress:0\", verdict=drop, severity=alert, direction=from-lport: tcp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:82:02:56,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:82:02:57,nw_src=10.130.2.86,nw_dst=10.130.2.87,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=64,nw_frag=no,tp_src=45614,tp_dst=8080,tcp_flags=syn\n2024-06-10T18:10:25.414Z|00019|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"BANP:default:Ingress:1\", verdict=drop, severity=alert, direction=to-lport: tcp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:82:02:58,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:82:02:56,nw_src=10.130.2.88,nw_dst=10.130.2.86,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=64,nw_frag=no,tp_src=40630,tp_dst=8080,tcp_flags=syn\n2024-06-10T18:10:26.457Z|00020|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"BANP:default:Ingress:1\", verdict=drop, severity=alert, direction=to-lport: tcp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:82:02:58,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:82:02:56,nw_src=10.130.2.88,nw_dst=10.130.2.86,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=64,nw_frag=no,tp_src=40630,tp_dst=8080,tcp_flags=syn\n2024-06-10T18:10:28.505Z|00021|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"BANP:default:Ingress:1\", verdict=drop, severity=alert, direction=to-lport: tcp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:82:02:58,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:82:02:56,nw_src=10.130.2.88,nw_dst=10.130.2.86,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=64,nw_frag=no,tp_src=40630,tp_dst=8080,tcp_flags=syn"} lang="text" />
      <Fragment set:html={"</details>\n"} />
      <p>The following table describes BANP annotation:</p>
      <p><em></em><em><strong>Audit logging BaselineAdminNetworkPolicy annotation</strong></em><em></em></p>
      <Fragment set:html={"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n  <th>Annotation</th>\n  <th>Value</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n  <td><code>k8s.ovn.org/acl-logging</code></td>\n  <td>You must specify at least one of <code>Allow</code> or <code>Deny</code> to enable audit logging for a namespace.<br><br><code>Deny</code>:: Optional: Specify <code>alert</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>notice</code>, <code>info</code>, or <code>debug</code>.<code>Allow</code>:: Optional: Specify <code>alert</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>notice</code>, <code>info</code>, or <code>debug</code>.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"} />
      <h2 id="nw-networkpolicy-audit-configure_logging-network-security" class="group scroll-mt-20">Configuring egress firewall and network policy auditing for a cluster<a href="#nw-networkpolicy-audit-configure_logging-network-security" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">To customize egress firewall and network policy audit logging in OpenShift Container Platform, you can configure the <code>policyAuditConfig</code> section in the cluster <code>Network</code> custom resource. Adjust log destination, file size, and rate limits to control how ACL events are recorded.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>Install the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>Log in to the cluster with a user with <code>cluster-admin</code> privileges.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      To customize the audit logging configuration, enter the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc edit network.operator.openshift.io/cluster"} lang="terminal" />
      <Alert variant="tip" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Tip</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>You can also customize and apply the following YAML to configure audit logging:</p>
          <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: operator.openshift.io/v1\nkind: Network\nmetadata:\n  name: cluster\nspec:\n  defaultNetwork:\n    ovnKubernetesConfig:\n      policyAuditConfig:\n        destination: \"null\"\n        maxFileSize: 50\n        rateLimit: 20\n        syslogFacility: local0"} lang="yaml" />
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      To create a namespace with network policies complete the following steps:
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create a namespace for verification:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ cat <<EOF| oc create -f -\nkind: Namespace\napiVersion: v1\nmetadata:\n  name: verify-audit-logging\n  annotations:\n    k8s.ovn.org/acl-logging: '{ \"deny\": \"alert\", \"allow\": \"alert\" }'\nEOF"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>Successful output lists the namespace with the network policy and the <code>created</code> status.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create network policies for the namespace:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ cat <<EOF| oc create -n verify-audit-logging -f -\napiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\nkind: NetworkPolicy\nmetadata:\n  name: deny-all\nspec:\n  podSelector:\n    matchLabels:\n  policyTypes:\n  - Ingress\n  - Egress\n---\napiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\nkind: NetworkPolicy\nmetadata:\n  name: allow-from-same-namespace\n  namespace: verify-audit-logging\nspec:\n  podSelector: {}\n  policyTypes:\n   - Ingress\n   - Egress\n  ingress:\n    - from:\n        - podSelector: {}\n  egress:\n    - to:\n       - namespaceSelector:\n          matchLabels:\n            kubernetes.io/metadata.name: verify-audit-logging\nEOF"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"networkpolicy.networking.k8s.io/deny-all created\nnetworkpolicy.networking.k8s.io/allow-from-same-namespace created"} lang="text" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create a pod for source traffic in the <code>default</code> namespace:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ cat <<EOF| oc create -n default -f -\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: client\nspec:\n  containers:\n    - name: client\n      image: registry.access.redhat.com/rhel7/rhel-tools\n      command: [\"/bin/sh\", \"-c\"]\n      args:\n        [\"sleep inf\"]\nEOF"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create two pods in the <code>verify-audit-logging</code> namespace:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ for name in client server; do\ncat <<EOF| oc create -n verify-audit-logging -f -\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: ${name}\nspec:\n  containers:\n    - name: ${name}\n      image: registry.access.redhat.com/rhel7/rhel-tools\n      command: [\"/bin/sh\", \"-c\"]\n      args:\n        [\"sleep inf\"]\nEOF\ndone"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>Successful output lists the two pods, such as <code>pod/client</code> and <code>pod/server</code>, and the <code>created</code> status.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
      To generate traffic and produce network policy audit log entries, complete the following steps:
      <ol>
      <li>
      Obtain the IP address for pod named <code>server</code> in the <code>verify-audit-logging</code> namespace:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ POD_IP=$(oc get pods server -n verify-audit-logging -o jsonpath='{.status.podIP}')"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Ping the IP address from an earlier command from the pod named <code>client</code> in the <code>default</code> namespace and confirm the all packets are dropped:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc exec -it client -n default -- /bin/ping -c 2 $POD_IP"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"PING 10.128.2.55 (10.128.2.55) 56(84) bytes of data.\n\n--- 10.128.2.55 ping statistics ---\n2 packets transmitted, 0 received, 100% packet loss, time 2041ms"} lang="text" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      From the client pod in the <code>verify-audit-logging</code> namespace, ping the IP address stored in the <code>POD_IP shell</code> environment variable and confirm the system allows all packets.
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc exec -it client -n verify-audit-logging -- /bin/ping -c 2 $POD_IP"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"PING 10.128.0.86 (10.128.0.86) 56(84) bytes of data.\n64 bytes from 10.128.0.86: icmp_seq=1 ttl=64 time=2.21 ms\n64 bytes from 10.128.0.86: icmp_seq=2 ttl=64 time=0.440 ms\n\n--- 10.128.0.86 ping statistics ---\n2 packets transmitted, 2 received, 0% packet loss, time 1001ms\nrtt min/avg/max/mdev = 0.440/1.329/2.219/0.890 ms"} lang="text" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      </li>
      <li>
      Display the latest entries in the network policy audit log:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ for pod in $(oc get pods -n openshift-ovn-kubernetes -l app=ovnkube-node --no-headers=true | awk '{ print $1 }') ; do\n    oc exec -it $pod -n openshift-ovn-kubernetes -- tail -4 /var/log/ovn/acl-audit-log.log\n  done"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"2023-11-02T16:28:54.139Z|00004|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"NP:verify-audit-logging:Ingress\", verdict=drop, severity=alert, direction=to-lport: tcp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:81:02:01,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:81:02:23,nw_src=10.131.0.39,nw_dst=10.129.2.35,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=62,nw_frag=no,tp_src=58496,tp_dst=8080,tcp_flags=syn\n2023-11-02T16:28:55.187Z|00005|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"NP:verify-audit-logging:Ingress\", verdict=drop, severity=alert, direction=to-lport: tcp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:81:02:01,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:81:02:23,nw_src=10.131.0.39,nw_dst=10.129.2.35,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=62,nw_frag=no,tp_src=58496,tp_dst=8080,tcp_flags=syn\n2023-11-02T16:28:57.235Z|00006|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"NP:verify-audit-logging:Ingress\", verdict=drop, severity=alert, direction=to-lport: tcp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:81:02:01,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:81:02:23,nw_src=10.131.0.39,nw_dst=10.129.2.35,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=62,nw_frag=no,tp_src=58496,tp_dst=8080,tcp_flags=syn\n2023-11-02T16:49:57.909Z|00028|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"NP:verify-audit-logging:allow-from-same-namespace:Egress:0\", verdict=allow, severity=alert, direction=from-lport: icmp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:81:02:22,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:81:02:23,nw_src=10.129.2.34,nw_dst=10.129.2.35,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=64,nw_frag=no,icmp_type=8,icmp_code=0\n2023-11-02T16:49:57.909Z|00029|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"NP:verify-audit-logging:allow-from-same-namespace:Ingress:0\", verdict=allow, severity=alert, direction=to-lport: icmp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:81:02:22,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:81:02:23,nw_src=10.129.2.34,nw_dst=10.129.2.35,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=64,nw_frag=no,icmp_type=8,icmp_code=0\n2023-11-02T16:49:58.932Z|00030|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"NP:verify-audit-logging:allow-from-same-namespace:Egress:0\", verdict=allow, severity=alert, direction=from-lport: icmp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:81:02:22,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:81:02:23,nw_src=10.129.2.34,nw_dst=10.129.2.35,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=64,nw_frag=no,icmp_type=8,icmp_code=0\n2023-11-02T16:49:58.932Z|00031|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"NP:verify-audit-logging:allow-from-same-namespace:Ingress:0\", verdict=allow, severity=alert, direction=to-lport: icmp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:81:02:22,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:81:02:23,nw_src=10.129.2.34,nw_dst=10.129.2.35,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=64,nw_frag=no,icmp_type=8,icmp_code=0\n"} lang="text" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <h2 id="nw-networkpolicy-audit-enable_logging-network-security" class="group scroll-mt-20">Enabling egress firewall and network policy audit logging for a namespace<a href="#nw-networkpolicy-audit-enable_logging-network-security" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">To enable egress firewall and network policy audit logging for a namespace in OpenShift Container Platform, you can add the <code>k8s.ovn.org/acl-logging</code> annotation with the <code>oc annotate</code> command. You can also apply a namespace YAML file that sets <code>Allow</code> and <code>Deny</code> log severity levels.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>Install the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>Log in to the cluster with a user with <code>cluster-admin</code> privileges.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      To enable audit logging for a namespace, enter the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc annotate namespace <namespace> \\\n  k8s.ovn.org/acl-logging='{ \"deny\": \"alert\", \"allow\": \"notice\" }'"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;namespace&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of the namespace.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      <Alert variant="tip" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Tip</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>You can also apply the following YAML to enable audit logging:</p>
          <CodeBlock code={"kind: Namespace\napiVersion: v1\nmetadata:\n  name: <namespace>\n  annotations:\n    k8s.ovn.org/acl-logging: |-\n      {\n        \"deny\": \"alert\",\n        \"allow\": \"notice\"\n      }"} lang="yaml" />
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <p>Successful output lists the audit logging name and the <code>annotated</code> status.</p>
      </li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Display the latest entries in the audit log:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ for pod in $(oc get pods -n openshift-ovn-kubernetes -l app=ovnkube-node --no-headers=true | awk '{ print $1 }') ; do\n    oc exec -it $pod -n openshift-ovn-kubernetes -- tail -4 /var/log/ovn/acl-audit-log.log\n  done"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"2023-11-02T16:49:57.909Z|00028|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"NP:verify-audit-logging:allow-from-same-namespace:Egress:0\", verdict=allow, severity=alert, direction=from-lport: icmp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:81:02:22,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:81:02:23,nw_src=10.129.2.34,nw_dst=10.129.2.35,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=64,nw_frag=no,icmp_type=8,icmp_code=0\n2023-11-02T16:49:57.909Z|00029|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"NP:verify-audit-logging:allow-from-same-namespace:Ingress:0\", verdict=allow, severity=alert, direction=to-lport: icmp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:81:02:22,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:81:02:23,nw_src=10.129.2.34,nw_dst=10.129.2.35,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=64,nw_frag=no,icmp_type=8,icmp_code=0\n2023-11-02T16:49:58.932Z|00030|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"NP:verify-audit-logging:allow-from-same-namespace:Egress:0\", verdict=allow, severity=alert, direction=from-lport: icmp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:81:02:22,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:81:02:23,nw_src=10.129.2.34,nw_dst=10.129.2.35,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=64,nw_frag=no,icmp_type=8,icmp_code=0\n2023-11-02T16:49:58.932Z|00031|acl_log(ovn_pinctrl0)|INFO|name=\"NP:verify-audit-logging:allow-from-same-namespace:Ingress:0\", verdict=allow, severity=alert, direction=to-lport: icmp,vlan_tci=0x0000,dl_src=0a:58:0a:81:02:22,dl_dst=0a:58:0a:81:02:23,nw_src=10.129.2.34,nw_dst=10.129.2.35,nw_tos=0,nw_ecn=0,nw_ttl=64,nw_frag=no,icmp_type=8,icmp_code=0\n"} lang="text" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="nw-networkpolicy-audit-disable_logging-network-security" class="group scroll-mt-20">Disabling egress firewall and network policy audit logging for a namespace<a href="#nw-networkpolicy-audit-disable_logging-network-security" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">To disable egress firewall and network policy audit logging for a namespace in OpenShift Container Platform, you can remove the <code>k8s.ovn.org/acl-logging</code> annotation with the <code>oc annotate</code> command. You can also apply a namespace YAML file that sets the annotation to <code>null</code>.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>Install the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>Log in to the cluster with a user with <code>cluster-admin</code> privileges.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      To disable audit logging for a namespace, enter the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc annotate --overwrite namespace <namespace> k8s.ovn.org/acl-logging-"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;namespace&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of the namespace.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      <Alert variant="tip" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Tip</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>You can also apply the following YAML to disable audit logging:</p>
          <CodeBlock code={"kind: Namespace\napiVersion: v1\nmetadata:\n  name: <namespace>\n  annotations:\n    k8s.ovn.org/acl-logging: null"} lang="yaml" />
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <p>Successful output lists the audit logging name and the <code>annotated</code> status.</p>
      </li>
      </ul>
